  "answer": "This has been requested before. Keyboard Manager remaps apply to every connected keyboard, so remapping or disabling a key for a faulty laptop keyboard also affects the external one. PowerToys can't currently limit remaps to one keyboard. #48312 is almost the same case: a faulty internal key that can't be disabled without disabling it on the external keyboard. #8242 and #30420 ask for per-device remapping, and #13918, #14685 and #9688 request related per-keyboard features. These are open feature requests, so add a thumbs-up or your use case to them rather than filing a new ticket. For now, the workaround in the related tickets is to turn Keyboard Manager off in PowerToys Settings when you use the keyboard that shouldn't be remapped. A faulty internal keyboard may need a driver or hardware fix, or disabling that device in Windows Device Manager."
 },
